This is **demo content** for layout evaluation. Replace it with your own writing.

## When a lookup is enough

If each row belongs to exactly one parent, use a one-to-many relationship with a lookup column.

{% callout type="note" %}
Lookups give you cascading behavior and simpler security reasoning than many-to-many.
{% /callout %}

## When you need many-to-many

Use N:N when rows on both sides can relate to many rows on the other, and the relationship itself has no attributes.

```javascript
// Example: query related rows with the Web API
const url = "/api/data/v9.2/accounts?$expand=contact_customer_accounts($select=fullname)";
```
